{"event":"changes_requested","job_id":"docs-marketplaces-compliance-financial-products-foreign-exchange-fees","reason":"The complete 101-line pinned raw matches the trusted SHA-256, all five quotations occur at their cited lines, and candidate and suggestions match the accepted receipt. The source and Q1/Q2 correctly retain the historical non-legal and all-region-as-Adyen-guidance qualifications, the inconsistent first fixed-fee table, and the distinction between illustrative intermediary-fee routes and actual beneficiary receipt. One material modal is softened: raw line 21 says users with any currency-conversion transaction 'must be clearly presented' the FX rate and additional fees at transaction time and in relevant statements, but the source Overview and first Key takeaway say the rate/fees 'should' be presented or seen. A reader asking whether disclosure can be optional could receive a weaker answer than the dated guide states. This is a bounded source-wording correction; no raw, quote, numerical warning or concept-route change is needed."}
