{"event":"changes_requested","job_id":"docs-marketplaces-compliance-financial-products-keeping-records","reason":"Independently read the complete pinned raw and verified its SHA-256, five exact located quotes, receipt/candidate/suggestions agreement, dated five-year offering-termination boundary, product-family route and Q1/Q2 coverage. One material compliance modal is flattened in the UK/IE vulnerable-customer takeaway: raw lines 29\u201332 say recording systems **must include the ability** to categorize signs of vulnerability, but **should include at least** the four listed categorization options. The candidate says systems 'should categorize ... using at least' the options, which weakens the mandatory capability and implies a different action."}
{"event":"changes_requested","job_id":"docs-payouts-payout-service-internal-fund-transfers","reason":"Independently read all 44 lines of the pinned raw and verified its SHA-256. Candidate and suggestions match the accepted receipt; all four quotes are exact at their cited lines. The source and Q1/Q2 correctly identify the Payout Service balance-account-to-balance-account purpose, scheduled/on-demand routes and external-bank boundary, and the reciprocal concept route exists. One source sentence says linked guides establish 'whether a particular transfer reached a booked state.' Static process guides can describe event semantics and evidence to inspect, but cannot establish the actual state of a particular transfer. That sentence undermines the otherwise clear execution-proof boundary for a completion query."}
